at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Logan County in northeastern Colorado...\nCentral Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nNorth Central Washington County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 645 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has\nfallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nBeaver Creek, Pawnee Creek, Bijou Creek, Wildcat Creek, Badger\nCreek, Kiowa Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch\nare expected over the area. This additional rain will result in\nminor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFort Morgan, Brush, Wiggins, Log Lane Village, Merino, Hillrose,\nSnyder, Prewitt Reservoir, Fort Morgan Airport, Union and Messex.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.56abaf26c235284d9caf2a8d5c5a3bb3400a5848.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.56abaf26c235284d9caf2a8d5c5a3bb3400a5848.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-17T00:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 170007 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 607 PM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and storms continue this evening, some strong to severe. Strong winds, hail, and heavy rain/flash flooding on the table. - Afternoon storms are expected again on Monday, mostly over the eastern mountains and Raton Mesa. - A bit drier through the rest of th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-16T17:21:00+00:00","snipp